  "question": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{HgI}_{4}$ is $40 \\%$ ionised in aqueous solution. The value of its van't Hoff factor (i) is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1.6",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1.8",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "20",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "22",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\mathrm{Hgl}_{4} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{~K}^{+}+\\left[\\mathrm{Hgl}_{4}\\right]^{2-} ; \\mathrm{n}=3$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\r\n\\because & \\alpha=\\frac{i-1}{n-1} ; 0.4=\\frac{\\mathrm{i}-1}{3-1} \\\\\r\n\r\n& i=1.8\r\n\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n\r\n$$"
  }
